{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["His tunic — like: בנו [ציפור] בנו [בעור], and מדיו קרועים — a term for garments." "And he shall lift up the ashes — [the terumah offering of ashes] — this is its commandment every day, before the morning tamid offering. But 'and he shall take out the ashes' — that is for an extended interval, to clear the altar of the abundance of ashes upon it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The first bracketed Hebrew words are rabbinic parallels illustrating the form מדו as a garment term; the third is a quoted phrase (Kings I 11:29) where the same root means garments."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:22.985345202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}